6 youths out of 10 arrested in case of violence against 2 youths in Takhmao City
(Central): Six out of 10 youths were arrested by the police force of Takhmao City Police Inspector after beating two youths, causing serious injuries.
The incident happened in front of Azotech Cafe in Takhmao Village, Sangkat Takhmao, Takhmao City, Kandal Province on April 10, 2023 at 16:30.
Regarding this case, Mr. Yi Vanda, Police Inspector of Takhmao City, said that this case caused violence because 10 young people were angry with the victim. One in six youths has been released due to their young age, while police are pursuing four other accomplices.
Sources said that after the incident, the authorities of Takhmao City chased and arrested six suspects and sent them to the inspectorate for questioning and legal action. But because one was too young, the prosecutor released him.
First: Name: Kour Kimseng, Male, 15 years old, Occupation: Student, Residence: Trapeang Chhouk Village, Sangkat O Bek Kam, Khan Sen Sok, Phnom Penh.
And 2: Nhao Nithi, male, 13 years old, living in Sonsom Kosal 2 Village, Sangkat Steung Meanchey, Khan Meanchey, Phnom Penh, with a scar on the back of his head.
The suspects are currently being held in custody at the Takhmao City Inspectorate to build a case for legal proceedings.
