At least 1.2 million people have been displaced by post-coup fighting, according to the United Nations.
Tuesday's incident could be one of the deadliest airstrikes since a Myanmar military plane bombed a concert in October, killing civilians, local singers and members of armed ethnic groups. At least 50 in Kachin State.
Ministry of Labor calls on factories to join World Day for Occupational Safety and Health
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training has announced the celebration of the World Day for Occupational Safety and Health and called on factories to participate in this World Day in order to promote occupational safety and health and to commemorate the souls of workers. Lost lives due to occupational accidents and occupational diseases around the world.
The World Day for Occupational Safety and Health is celebrated on April 28 every year by the member countries of the International Labor Organization.
This is the 18th year that the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training will celebrate the World Day for Occupational Safety and Health under the theme "Safe Work Environment and Occupational Health" is a fundamental right and principle in the workplace, which will take place on the 28th. April 2023 in Phnom Penh Special Economic Zone, with participants from relevant institutions, employers' representatives, union representatives and a total of 1,300 workers.
In order to contribute to the promotion and promotion of occupational safety and health and the prevention of occupational accidents and occupational diseases eventually to the workers, all owners or directors of factories located in Cambodia should put up banners and slogans along the fence. In front of the factory to celebrate the World Day for Occupational Safety and Health are as follows:
1. Celebrate World Day for Occupational Safety and Health April 28
2. A safe and healthy work environment is a basic right and principle in the workplace.
3. Take joint action to build a positive culture, safety and occupational health
4. Establish occupational safety and health management system in all workplaces
5. Safe work is no work accident
6. Ensure that all workplaces in the Kingdom of Cambodia are safe
7. Together to reduce occupational accidents and occupational diseases
9. A decent job is a safe job. The Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training strongly hopes that the Capital-Provincial Departments of Labor and Vocational Training, employers' associations and owners or directors, as well as all trade union federations of factories will comply with this notice effectively.
