ASEAN Secretary-General Dr. Kao Kim Hourn Continues to Meet with Foreign Leaders After Inauguration
(Jakarta, Indonesia): Dr. Kao Kim Hourn, Secretary-General of ASEAN, who was officially inaugurated recently, received a series of talks with a number of foreign leaders.
* Third: On the afternoon of Tuesday, April 11, 2023, Dr. Kao Kim Hourn met with Mr. Erin Cornelli, Senior Officer in charge of Southeast Asian Policy and Foreign Policy for the International Institute for Strategic Studies (IISS).
During the meeting, the two sides exchanged views on regional and global developments and discussed preparations for the 20th Sangkilla Dialogue, scheduled for early June 2023 in Singapore.
* Fourth: Dr. Kao Kim Hourn met with US Senator Jeff Merkel. During the meeting, the two sides exchanged views on various issues happening in the region and the world, especially to make the region more peaceful and prosperous. The ASEAN Secretary-General has stated that he will continue to work closely with the United States as a comprehensive strategic partner.
* Fifth: Dr. Kao Kim Hourn met with Mr. Teng Sichun, Special Envoy of China in charge of Asia. During the meeting, Dr. Kao Kim Hourn reiterated the readiness of the ASEAN Secretariat to continue working closely with ASEAN Member States and ASEAN Dialogue Partners, including China, to enhance cooperation. The two sides also discussed and exchanged views on cooperation between ASEAN and China.
Please be informed that Mr. Kao Kim Hourn has been appointed as the Secretary General of ASEAN to replace Mr. Lim Chok Hoy, who ended his term on the afternoon of January 9, 2023 under the chairmanship of the Minister of Foreign Affairs of Indonesia.
