National Road Safety Committee issues appeal on road traffic accident prevention on the occasion of New Year
(Phnom Penh): The National Committee for Road Safety has issued an appeal on the prevention of road accidents on the occasion of the traditional New Year from 14 to 16 April 2023. This is according to the appeal received by Fresh News on April 11, 2023.
According to the appeal of the National Road Safety Committee, we would like to express our deepest gratitude to the vast majority of road users who are willing to respect and enforce the law on road traffic during traffic. Contribute to reducing the loss of life, injuries and property damage caused by road accidents in the past.
In a situation where the country is completely peaceful and operates in all areas along the new normal trajectory after the Kovid-19 pandemic has eased, road traffic across the country has become busier and the number of vehicles has increased. Every year. With this, as well as the challenges posed by road accidents still occur every day, high growth during the festival.
On the occasion of the traditional New Year, which will take place from 14 to 16 April 2023, the National Committee for Road Safety calls on all road users to pay attention. Apply to prevent and prevent road traffic accidents by the following measures:
May all road users adhere to the law on road traffic to protect their own lives, for the harmony of the family, to protect your property and to jointly promote the honor and dignity of our nation. But there is development in all areas.
The National Road Safety Committee hopes that all road users will abide by the implementation of the Road Traffic Law, as well as follow this call with a high sense of responsibility to bring safety and security. Happy on the occasion of the upcoming National New Year and will continue forever.
