(Phnom Penh): Phnom Penh Governor Khuon Sreng urged officials and relevant departments to restore the Choeung Ek canal quickly and widely to bring water out of the capital as soon as the rainy season arrives.
Mr. Khuong Sreng's urging was made this morning, April 11, 2023, as he led the authorities and departments to inspect the condition of the Choeung Ek canal so that the team can work on the mud and expand the canal. Before and make the water flow faster.
Mr. Khuong Sreng said, "We have four months to work on this canal, especially in the dry season." In the dry season, it is easy for us to restore as well as expand the canal body, so that when the rainy season arrives, we can push water out of Phnom Penh quickly, reducing the flooding of people's homes in Phnom Penh.
Mr. Sam Piseth, Director of the Department of Public Works and Transport of Phnom Penh, confirmed that the Choeung Ek Canal has a very important role in releasing water from Phnom Penh by flowing to Boeung Trabek Station, which is about 12 kilometers from Boeung Trabek Station through the district. Meanchey, Dangkor district, continues to Stung Chrov village in Doeum Mean commune, Takhmao city, Kandal province.
Mr. Sam Piseth continued that according to the instructions of Mr. Khuong Sreng, it is required for the team to restore and excavate the canal to a width of 20 meters to 60 meters, depending on the actual situation. The team must continue to carry out this work regularly and be completed before the rainy season arrives, which means that when the rainy season arrives, the canal must play an important role in releasing water from Phnom Penh well.
