Taiwan claims eight Chinese warships continue to operate in waters around its islands
BEIJING (Reuters) - Eight Chinese warships continued to operate in waters around Taiwan a day after Beijing closed its large-scale military exercises, the Defense Ministry said on Tuesday. This was released by the AFP news agency on Tuesday, April 11, 2023.
China held a three-day military exercise around Taiwan, starting last Saturday and ending on Monday, with the Chinese military rehearsing how to attack and blockade Taiwan. The exercise is in response to a meeting between Taiwanese leader Sai Ying-jeou and US House of Representatives Speaker Kevin McCarthy in California last week.
In a statement, the Taiwanese Defense Ministry confirmed that eight Chinese warships were still operating in waters around Taiwan, and that the Taiwanese military was currently monitoring their activities.
