Senior Minister Osman Hassan pays a courtesy call on Saudi Arabia's Ambassador to Cambodia
During the meeting, Dr. Osman Hassan thanked the Royal Government of Saudi Arabia for facilitating Cambodian Muslims to receive scholarships, build temples, schools and perform Hajj obligations.
At the same time, Dr. also requested the Saudi side to further facilitate the increase in the number of pilgrims (pilgrims) for Cambodia so that Cambodian Muslims have the opportunity to perform more pilgrimages to fulfill their obligations. This is important. He also called for Cambodia's support in applying for membership in the Organization of Islamic Cooperation (OIC), the second largest organization after the United Nations.
In addition, he also mentioned the momentum of development in all sectors in Cambodia, such as trade, tourism, agriculture, education, humanitarian and other sectors. He also asked the Saudi side to cooperate and promote the people, entrepreneurs, investors of Saudi Arabia to invest in various sectors, including halal, agriculture and industry, Cambodia is ready to cooperate with Saudi Arabia. Udit.
Mr. Osman Hassan also mentioned the policy of the Royal Government of Cambodia, which has harmonized race and religion in Cambodia. In particular, the Muslim community also receives attention and offers community representatives to become leaders in the Senate, National Assembly, Royal Government, Secretary of State, Undersecretary of State, senior diplomats, national and sub-national authorities, and all armed forces. Types and civil servants.
He said that the Saudi side is really working to open an embassy in Cambodia to strengthen closer cooperation in all fields, especially Hajj (pilgrimage). As for investing in Cambodia, he said he would study more to encourage his country's investors to invest in Cambodia.
Please be informed that Cambodia-Saudi Arabia achieved bilateral trade amounting to 26 million US dollars in 2021, an increase of nearly 40% compared to 2020 (only 19 million US dollars), while bilateral trade amounted to 15 million US dollars. $ 6 million in 2019 and $ 16 million in 2018. This is according to the Ministry of Commerce of Cambodia.
