(Phnom Penh): The Russey Keo cable-stayed bridge, which crosses the 6th river in Phnom Penh, was temporarily opened to the public on the morning of April 10, 2023.
The Russey Keo Concrete Bridge across the Tonle Sap River connecting National Roads 6 and 5 in Khan Chroy Changva and Khan Russey Keo, Phnom Penh, was opened in October 2017 under the presidency of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia. The bridge was built by the Cambodian Overseas Investment Company (OCIC) of Duke Pong Khieu Se.
The Russey Keo concrete bridge has four lanes, two lanes and two lanes. The bridge was built by a Cambodian architect and is the first cable-stayed bridge in Phnom Penh to be built using cable in the center. Through this cable is highlighted by colored lights, which makes the bridge more beautiful at night.
Mr. Sam Piseth, Director of the Department of Public Works and Transport of Phnom Penh, thanked the team of engineers and workers who worked together to achieve this beautiful achievement in Phnom Penh.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen allowed people to cross the bridge temporarily to facilitate people's travel as well as avoid traffic jams during the New Year.
The Russey Keo Concrete Bridge is another new achievement in Phnom Penh under the shadow of peace and development efforts of the Royal Government led by Samdech Techo Prime Minister. This historic achievement in the territory of Phnom Penh made the people express their joy.
The Russey Keo concrete bridge facilitates the movement of people between National Road No. 5 and No. 6 without having to spend time crossing the Chroy Changvar Bridge. On the morning of April 10, after the bridge was opened, many people passed by with happy faces.
Some residents who have houses near the bridge, even though they do not have the duty to cross the bridge, have come to appreciate this new achievement.
The people who traveled across the new bridge on Phnom Penh were all excited and happy. They expressed their deep gratitude to Samdech Techo for building new achievements to meet the needs of the people.
