(Phnom Penh): Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Economy and Finance, shared seven key points of view with indications on some key issues as input for the discussion. Education is getting better.
This morning, April 10, 2023, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, presided over the opening ceremony of a conference to review education, youth and sports in the 2021-2022 school year and directions. For the academic year 2022-2023.
The views of Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth in the opening ceremony of the conference to summarize the work of education, youth and sports are as follows:
First, improving the quality of education at all levels is a top priority, especially at the primary level, to ensure that students have a strong foundation and are capable enough to continue their education to secondary and tertiary levels with confidence in response to The urgency of the need for quality human capital.
Second, improving the quality of teaching, learning and research, and expanding new subjects and skills in higher education is another major priority in response to the current and future socio-economic developments.
Third, improving the quality of education requires strengthening governance and management efficiency in the Department of Education, Youth and Sports and schools at all levels, as well as promoting the involvement of parents, communities and the private sector.
Fourth, to strengthen the training of teachers and staff, as well as to continue to improve the lives, abilities and values of teachers to be worthy of Cambodia's leading force in building human capital towards achieving the vision of Cambodia 2050. An increasingly important task, especially in the context of new normal education.
In addition, Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth also expressed the hope that this conference will turn the above priorities into specific action plans to achieve educational goals with clear performance indicators.
He also supported the prioritization of results-oriented activities and the implementation of education reforms focused on system building and capacity development, and affirmed that these tasks really respond to the work of key reform work. Of the Royal Government of Cambodia as stated in the Rectangular Strategy - Phase 4, as well as considering the strategic framework for the new Royal Government in the upcoming 7th legislature.
