Minister Vong Soth: The social sector has played an important role in helping the victims and vulnerable groups of former civil servants and veterans
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Vong Soth, Minister of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation, said that starting from this, the social sector, veterans and youth rehabilitation has played an important role and achieved many new achievements, including the implementation of program policies. National Social Welfare aims to create public services to help victims and vulnerable groups, former civil servants, veterans and social protection to the people.
Mr. Vong Soth made the remarks while addressing the meeting to review the work results of 2022 and the direction of implementation of 2023 of the Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation on April 10, 2023.
At the same time, Minister Vong Soth commended the relevant ministries, institutions, authorities, the private sector, national and international organizations and development partners at both the national and sub-national levels for their past cooperation in implementing the Ministry's strategic plan to promote Social work, especially the provision of social services closer to the people in accordance with the actual needs and policies of the Royal Government that have been implemented.
Mr. Vong Soth said that the progress made by the Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation in the past is due to the high commitment of all levels of government officials and good cooperation from relevant ministries, institutions, local authorities, partner organizations and philanthropists. I congratulate you on this noble achievement.
The Minister of Social Affairs added that in addition to the important achievements mentioned above, we still have many challenges that require us to continue to work together to find solutions such as climate change, outbreaks, migration. Homes, homelessness, human trafficking, labor trafficking, sexual exploitation, drug use, and demographic change.
In order to address these challenges, the Minister requested to continue to work on some additional tasks as follows:
1-Prepare and launch social assistance programs as a family package through the integration of integrated social assistance programs, including cash support programs for pregnant women and children under 2 years old, cash support programs for the disabled, adult support programs Alumni and cash support programs for poor students in the village.
2. To formulate a national social policy to determine the vision, priorities, work and responsibilities of all relevant actors in order to contribute to alleviating difficulties, raising the living standards, dignity and honor of the people.
3. To complete the preparation of the draft law and related legal documents in accordance with the planned program, especially the procedures and procedures for the transfer, transfer and reception of minors in conflict with the law to stay in the education center. Rehabilitate youth quickly.
