This afternoon, Samdech Techo Hun Sen Invites Conversation and Solidarity Dinner with Small and Medium Enterprise Owners
(Phnom Penh): On Monday afternoon, April 10, 2023, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, will hold a get-together with the owners of small and medium enterprises as well as business people in Cambodia. The event will be held at the Koh Pich Convention and Exhibition Center.
The event was also attended by about 5,000 national and international guests, including Vice Chairman, Board Member, Collaborators of Samdech Techo Foundation Association, President of FASMEC Branch in partner provinces, NGOs, partner banks, companies and enterprises. Small and medium and Cambodian handicrafts from 25 capitals and provinces.
This afternoon's Solidarity Meeting and Dinner demonstrates Samdech Techo Hun Sen's high concern for business people and small and medium enterprise owners in Cambodia, which is an important sector for the national economy.
This sector has contributed to the development of the national economy and increased employment for Cambodians throughout the country. In addition, small and medium enterprises and handicrafts are considered the backbone of the national economy, of which more than 90 percent of enterprises in Cambodia are small and medium enterprises and handicrafts, which provide more than 70 percent employment, equivalent to about 58 percent. Gross domestic product.
Currently, there are more than 700,000 small and medium enterprises and handicrafts in Cambodia, of which the manufacturing sector accounts for about 7%, equivalent to more than 40,000 bases, and most of them are about 80% food processing. The large factory has nearly 2,000 bases.
Recognizing the importance of small and medium enterprises, the Royal Government of Cambodia has released a number of budgets to support their activities during the Kovid 19 crisis.
To address the hardships caused by Kovid 19, the Royal Government of Cambodia has released a special $ 50 million package to the Rural Development and Agriculture Bank, establishing a $ 100 million co-financing project in equal portions between SME Bank and the Banking and Financial Institutions. Participated 33 and provided $ 200 million to establish a Cambodian Credit Guarantee Corporation.
