In a press release from the General Secretariat of the Senate, which Fresh News received, it was stated that the meeting proceeded with one agenda item.
The following is a press release from the General Secretariat of the Senate: Mr. HUN Many: Angkor Sankranti always has strong support from young volunteers, which is the main force in pushing for a great event to run smoothly.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Hun Many, President of the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia (UYFC), sent about 500 young volunteers this morning, April 10, 2023, on their way from Phnom Penh to Siem Reap to prepare for the upcoming Angkor Sankranti event. There are still young volunteers who will leave the next day.
Mr. Hun Many said, "Angkor Sankranti has always been strongly supported by the youth volunteers, who are the main force in pushing for a great event to run smoothly. From year to year, Angkor Sankranti is guided by the principle of voluntary participation of young people everywhere, who have been working on this project since the planning, implementation and leadership of the group in many sub-sections. .
It should be noted that the volunteer work of Angkor Sankranti event has created opportunities for a total of 5,000 young people to participate in social work, which is a good learning opportunity for them to develop both hard skills (performing, playing popular games) and Soft skills (team leadership, communication, problem solving).
