Koh Kong Provincial Police Commissioner Orders All Police Forces to Prepare Enough Properties and Materials to Protect People on New Year's Day
(Koh Kong): Major General Kong Mono, Koh Kong Provincial Police Commissioner, on April 10, 2023, inspected the police force and ordered all police forces to be adequately equipped and equipped to protect the safety of the people. National-international tourists on a traditional Khmer New Year trip.
Lt. Gen. Kong Mono stated that in order to comply with the order of the Ministry of Interior and the instructions of the provincial governor to protect the safety of people, national and international guests on the occasion of the traditional New Year, all forces are ready and equipped. Enough to protect the safety of people when they encounter any incident, including ambulances, fire trucks, motorbikes and other equipment.
He added that all royal forces in all districts and districts up to the local administrative post must be on duty 24 hours a day and to maintain order and facilitate traffic to prevent any crime from occurring on both waterways and land. .
He called on the people, both national and international guests, to respect the traffic law, to understand each other, to favor each other, to love solidarity and to help each other in times of emergency.
