Police arrest 4 people for stealing grandfather's money and jewelry totaling more than 10,000 USD to buy motorcycles and mobile phones for friends in Tram Kak district, Takeo province
(Phnom Penh): Police in Tram Kak district, Takeo province, conducted a search and arrested four suspects after an elderly man filed a lawsuit against his grandson for stealing more than $ 10,000. Including two necklaces on April 2, 2023.
Duk Thiya, Tram Kak district police inspector, said that the incident happened at Moha Sena village, Taphem commune, Tram Kak district, Takeo province.
After receiving the complaint and receiving the victim's complaint, there was a case where the suspect armed with a knife broke the door of the house and the desk drawer of a 69-year-old man named Uy Mao, Moha Sena village, Taphem commune, and took materials including gold necklaces. Two strings of $ 14,500 escaped when his grandparents and family left for Chheng Meng.
Immediately, the police conducted a search under the order of the Provincial Police Commissioner and coordinated by the Takeo Provincial Prosecutor on April 08, 2023. The specialized force of the District Police Inspectorate led by Mr. Duk Thiya in cooperation with the Commissioner Force. Preah Sihanouk Provincial Police and Kampot Provincial Police arrested these suspects.
The other three accomplices who received the stolen goods were 17-year-old Ing Sopheanut, 17-year-old Ren Chan You and 17-year-old Heng Makara.
Currently, the criminal police force of Tram Kak District Police Inspectorate is questioning and building a case to send the suspects to court for legal action.
