(Thailand): It is not only in Cambodia that Sankranti is a popular game to celebrate the traditional Khmer New Year in Thailand, but also many workers, students, business people and Cambodians. This is in the presence of Dr. Ith Sam Heng, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training and Chairman of the Commission for Legalization of Cambodian workers staying and working in Thailand.
This happy Sankranti ceremony is held at the Cambodian Embassy in the Kingdom of Thailand.
On that occasion, Dr. Ith Sam Heng conveyed the greetings and best wishes from Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Katiprit Dr. Bun Rany Hun Sen to all Cambodians who always take care of their well-being. Of our fellow workers working abroad.
Dr. Ith Sam Heng emphasized that Khmer New Year Sangkant is a big national tradition of Khmer Buddhists who have been in the hearts of all Cambodians since ancient times. This year, some of our Cambodian brothers and sisters in Thailand visited their hometowns for the New Year, but most of them did not visit the district because they were busy with work, but we have organized the traditional Khmer New Year here and can contact them to wish them a Happy New Year. New to the rich in our homeland.
The Minister commended the Ambassador and his colleagues for their efforts in fulfilling their diplomatic duties in accordance with the Royal Government's policy of strengthening good-neighborly cooperation between Cambodia and Thailand in the fields of economy, education, employment and providing opportunities for students to study. And provide employment opportunities for our Cambodian workers as well.
The Minister considered the cooperation between Cambodia and Thailand as a win-win cooperation, in which the Cambodian workers can find a job with income, know the skills that are working when returning home can take these skills to feed the team. Families will participate in national economic development. On the other hand, the country receives them labor to complete their production.
At the same time, Dr. Ith Sam Heng praised our Cambodian workers who have the spirit of perseverance, hard work, earning a living and contributing to the national income. "There are 1.2 million workers in Thailand, each sending home 167 US dollars a month, about 2 billion US dollars a year," he said.
The Minister instructed the workers to take care of their health, solidarity, and to respect the laws of their country well, to avoid committing wrongdoing.
During the upcoming National Assembly election on July 23, 2023, our workers have the same right to vote, to vote at the place where you are registered. His Excellency appealed to our workers as well as their families to vote. To the Cambodian People's Party to maintain peace and lead the country to further development and progress.
