(Phnom Penh): The Phnom Penh Municipal Court on April 10 will announce the verdict on the perpetrator of the accident that hit a man who killed three children and his wife two years ago, while the victim has not received any compensation.
The perpetrator who drove a car and hit a man, killing three children and his wife on February 22, 2021 in Chak Angre Leu commune, Meanchey district, Phnom Penh, was arrested by the police on December 26, 2022.
The arrest was made following an arrest warrant issued by Phnom Penh Municipal Court Investigating Judge Sin Sovannaroth. Defendant Men Ong, 39, resides in Keo Kamleung village, Prey Khla commune, Koh Andet district, Takeo province.
The Investigating Judge charged Men Ong with "reckless driving, negligence, causing death" at the intersection of Street 2 and Borey Chea Rattanak in Chak Angre Leu Sangkat, Khan Meanchey, Phnom Penh.
Earlier reports said that after the arrest of the perpetrator, Men Ong was immediately being intervened so that he could be released on bail.
