Mr. You Serey Vuth and Mr. Phen Phalla Meet with 420 Workers in Kandal Province
(Kandal): Mr. You Serey Vuth, Chairman of the Working Group on Party Members in Factory Workers in Kandal Province, and Mr. Phen Phalla, Assistant to Samdech Techo, President of the Cambodian People's Party, together with the working group, visited and talked with about 420 people.
The get-together took place on the afternoon of April 08, 2023 at Floris Garment Company in Sdao Kanleang Village, Dei Edth Commune, Kien Svay District, Kandal Province.
During the meeting, Mr. You Serey Vuth and Mr. Phen Phalla expressed their warm welcome to the presence of all workers taking part in the event.
The Chairman and Deputy Chairman of the Working Group on Building Party Members in the Factory Workers in Kandal Province brought Samdech Techo Hun Sen's greetings and greetings to all the participating workers.
In the friendly atmosphere, Mr. You Sereyvuth and Mr. Phen Phalla highlighted the success of the Royal Government led by Samdech Techo in overcoming the Kovid 19 pandemic. In particular, the release of a national budget package to help workers who lost their jobs during the 19 19 outbreak of Kovid.
In particular, Mr. Phen Phalla reminded that in the 19 epidemic of Kovid, many workers lost their jobs. But the thoughtful spirit of the Prime Minister has released a monthly allowance package for workers, although not much, but also help workers solve difficulties in their daily lives.
In addition, You Serey Vuth and Phen Phalla also highlighted the global crisis caused by the 19-year-old Kovid and the war in Ukraine, which led to a drop in orders and the loss of some workers.
Mr. You Sereyvuth and Mr. Phen Phalla emphasized that these job losses were not due to the EBA issue as some people have suggested. The chairman and deputy chairman of the working group to build party members in the ranks of factory workers in Kandal province called on workers not to believe the propaganda of some people that the loss of jobs due to the loss of EBA.
"As long as the war in Ukraine is not over, the economic crisis will continue and jobs in the textile and garment sector will continue to suffer due to declining orders, unlike before the war," he said. "So the disruption in our country is not due to the EBA." This is the confirmation of Mr. You Sereyvuth.
However, Mr. You Sereyvuth and Mr. Phen Phalla encouraged all workers not to worry about these issues, because Samdech Techo, together with the leadership as a staff, has set out a number of strategies to solve all these problems to ensure That people still have jobs to earn a living.
Phnom Penh Authority Temporarily Brings the Russey Keo Concrete Bridge Across the Tonle Sap River in Chroy Changva and Russey Keo Districts for People to Travel for the New Year
(Phnom Penh): The Phnom Penh Capital Administration on April 9, 2023 issued a notification on the temporary commissioning of the Russey Keo concrete bridge across the Tonle Sap River in Khan Chroy Changva and Khan Russey Keo, Phnom Penh and closed to traffic across the bridge. Russey Keo.
The Phnom Penh Municipal Administration said that the construction of the Russey Keo concrete bridge across the Tonle Sap River in Chroy Changva and Russey Keo districts of Phnom Penh was opened in October 2017 under the highest presidency of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia. By Cambodia Overseas Investment Company (OCIC). Currently, construction is almost complete and there is still a small amount of work left that does not affect the temporary opening of traffic.
(Banteay Meanchey): After traffic accidents occurred too often along Street 160 at the intersection of four roads into the school in Kork Ampil village, O'Prat commune, Mongkul Borei district, Mr. Ly Sary, Deputy Governor of Banteay Meanchey province on April 08, 2023 The team put up four traffic signs at four intersections to enter these schools.
Mr. Ly Sary said that after receiving information from local authorities that traffic accidents occurred frequently at four intersections at O'Prasat Primary School, at the request of Mr. Sok Chantha, Director of the Provincial Department of Public Works and Transport, provided four traffic signs. Two 4-meter-high steel poles and poles, two cross-road student signs and two deceleration signs.
He said that after receiving four traffic signs, the experts in cooperation with the authorities seized two poles, one of which had students crossing the road and speed limit signs on the right and left side of the road. From four intersections, about 100 meters, for passengers driving motorcycles and cars to see slow down for students and residents to prevent traffic accidents.
Mr. Ly Sary instructed drivers across all four intersections to obey the traffic rules and not to drive in an accident, especially on roads with student signs and speed limit signs with students crossing. Attend school must be delayed or stopped for students to pass, must not drive at high speeds, must obey all traffic laws to prevent traffic accidents.
