8 cows were killed by lightning in the middle of the night in Boribo district, Kampong Chhnang province
(Kampong Chhnang): Eight cows were killed by lightning in the middle of the night in Kampong Ou village, Khun Rang commune, Baribo district, Kampong Chhnang province.
The village chief of Kampong Ou said by telephone that at 1:00 AM on April 8, 2023, there was a heavy rain and wind mixed with thunder, causing 08 cows to sleep. Inside the barn, lightning struck and killed people on the spot.
The village chief confirmed that there were more than 20 cows in the barn, but 8 were killed by lightning, and there was no danger.
He added that all the cows are their owners in Serey village in Khon Rang commune, and the owners have made a barn to sleep in front of Kampong Ou pagoda, which is more than 2 kilometers away from the owner's house for convenience and herding.
The owner of the cow is very sorry about this, but this is a natural disaster that can not be predicted. The loss of eight cows is also a huge loss for farmers in Sre Chamkar district.
As an authority, I would like to express my condolences to the owners of the cows and call on all the people in the rural villages to be careful because the rainy season is approaching. Rain, thunder, lightning and strong winds are very fierce, so everyone must be careful.
