Mr. Net Pheaktra made this remark at a press conference on the second phase of the Zero Trap Campaign on April 6, 2023 at the Pursat Provincial Department of Environment.
"The Ministry of Environment and WA and India are working together to develop technical standards for the importation of large species from India to increase the number of rare species in Cambodia," the spokesman said. . The first direction is towards the Cardamom Mountains.
At the same time, Mr. Neth Pheaktra said that in Cambodia, there was a big tiger, whose presence was last seen in 2007, which was recorded in the wildlife sanctuary of Mondulkiri province as of 2023. It has been 16 years since the presence of the big tiger, which can be concluded that Cambodia has become extinct. The extinct Cambodian big tiger may have been trapped.
Regarding the project to restore a large presence in the natural forest of Cambodia, Mr. Neth Pheaktra highlighted that the Royal Government of Cambodia has provided technical support in collaboration with the Government of India to bring big tiger species to Cambodia.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra emphasized: "We expect the procedure to be completed in the future ...! And an expert from the Ministry of Environment, a representative of the WA, also traveled to India to study, and the work process will evolve step by step, and hopefully our country will be able to restore this species of big tiger in our natural forest. "Again."
On that occasion, Mr. Neth Pheaktra said that the Ministry of Environment hopes to believe that the project will be successful after an agreement with the Government of India to implement this project.
The executive director of the Wildlife Alliance (WA), Dr. Suvanna Gonlet, had previously said that the big tigers to be brought from India would be released in the Cardamom Mountains, an area of zero traps. Equipped with surveillance cameras by conservation officials.
Please be informed that on November 12, 2022, Cambodia and India signed a Memorandum of Understanding on Cooperation in Biodiversity Conservation, Sustainable Wildlife Management and Strategies to Restore Big Tigers and Their Habitats in Cambodia.
The project restores the Big Tiger after disappearing from Cambodia during 2007, while around the world in 2010 it was estimated that there were about 3,200 big tigers, a decrease of 95. The percentage compared to the number that was in the early 20s is about 100,000. Minister of Post and Ambassador of Japan Celebrates New Year with Cambodian Alumni Association from Japan
The entertainment program of the Cambodian Alumni Association from Japan took place on the night of April 7, 2023 at the Cambodiana Hotel. On that occasion, Mr. Vakora, President of the Cambodian Alumni Association from Japan JAC, said that this year's Khmer New Year is very special because it coincides with the 70th anniversary of diplomatic relations between Cambodia and Japan and the 20th anniversary. +1 of the Cambodian Alumni Association from Japan.
He added that JAC has a vision to establish and strengthen alliances with overseas alumni associations to create a network of potential professionals and promote development in Cambodia.
At the same time, the Ambassador of Japan, Eno Aatsushi, said that after the end of the civil war in Cambodia, Japan has continued to accept Cambodian students to study in their country under the Japanese Government Scholarship Program since 1992. For the past 30 years, more than 1,400 Cambodian students have studied in Japan, including students under the Japan People's Fund for Human Resource Development (JDS) in Cambodia.
On the occasion of the 70th anniversary of the establishment of diplomatic relations between Japan and Cambodia, both sides made efforts to maintain historical and friendly relations with each other, especially through the Cambodian Alumni Association (JAC).
At the same time, Minister Chea Vandeth also thanked for the promotion of friendly relations between Cambodia and Japan and celebrated the 70th anniversary of diplomatic relations between Cambodia and Japan, as well as the 20th anniversary of JAC.
The Minister said that the Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications also has a number of senior officials who have graduated from Japan in the field of Information Technology, Posts and Telecommunications. Together with other talented officials, they developed more than 18 technology systems for the ministry's internal use involving financial and real estate management systems as an interesting pilot model.
Please be informed that in addition to the above speech, the ceremony also organized the writing of Japanese characters (kanji), handing over souvenirs, debating and receiving solidarity food, playing Khmer folk games and dancing in the traditional Khmer style. Also. Ratanakkiri Provincial Health Department and partners launch awareness campaign on childbirth and increase immunization for children under 5
(Ratanakkiri): The Ratanakkiri Provincial Health Department, in collaboration with the Kiri Project, launched a joint march to raise awareness of community members and raise awareness among pregnant women about the importance of prenatal and postpartum care and vaccination. For children under 5 years old.
This important campaign was held on the morning of April 7, 2023 under the chairmanship of Mr. Duch Chanto, Deputy Governor of Ratanakkiri Province and Mr. Ung Ratana, Director of Ratanakkiri Provincial Health Department, as well as many other relevant officials.
Dr. Ung Ratana said that the campaign aims to spread knowledge to people in the community, especially to raise awareness among pregnant women about the importance of prenatal health care during pregnancy. Postpartum health and promote immunization for children under 5 years of age.
He said the project also aims to improve the quality of maternal and child health services, improve access to health services and raise community awareness.
The Deputy Governor appealed to all pregnant mothers to go to the health center at least 4 times before giving birth and after giving birth to go to the health center 10 times and take the baby. 11 vaccines were also given.
He thanked Korea for its financial support for the project, which has made a further contribution to strengthening the health system in Ratanakkiri province.
