Health Minister: Over the past two decades, the infant mortality rate has dropped rapidly from 37 to 8 per 1,000 live births.
(Phnom Penh): Professor Mam Bunheng, Minister of Health, said that in the past two decades, the infant mortality rate has dropped rapidly from 37 to eight per 1,000 live births.
This statement was made by the Minister of Health on the occasion of closing the workshop to review the results of the implementation of the roadmap for accelerating the reduction of maternal and infant mortality 2016-2020 and the celebration of the 75th anniversary of the World Health Organization in This April 7, 2023 at the Phnom Penh Hotel.
He added that the Royal Government of Cambodia, under the wise leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, has taken great care of the well-being of all Cambodians.
On that occasion, Minister Mam Bunheng also urged the relevant officials to jointly speed up the preparation of a digital system to monitor the health of newborns to adults. The establishment of this digital infant health monitoring system will also contribute to improving infant health and reducing infant and child mortality in Cambodia.
At the same time, the Minister also called on the World Health Organization and all development partners to continue to help more resources, spirit and new technologies on reproductive health, mothers, infants, children and youth health to achieve sustainable development goals.
