Samdech Techo Hun Sen Calls on People to Participate in Preventing and Reducing the Death and Injury Due to Traffic Accidents (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Citizens are involved in preventing and reducing the number of deaths and injuries caused by traffic accidents across the country to a minimum.
According to the results of the meeting of the Council of Ministers, in that meeting, Samdech Techo also called on the relevant ministries and institutions to promote the dissemination and mainstreaming of educational content related to traffic safety widely and through special public forums. Implementing traffic safety in the village-commune-sangkat safety policy.
It should be noted that in this morning's meeting, the Council of Ministers also approved the draft National Plan for the Road Safety Action Decade 2021-2030.
This draft national plan is the second national plan from the first national plan 2011-2020, which was implemented in the past to contribute to the successful implementation of the Royal Government's political program in accordance with the national policy on traffic safety. Roads and which have been coordinated in accordance with the United Nations Global Action Plan based on the Road Traffic Law in response to national progress in all areas, especially those related to road traffic activities.
The draft National Road Safety Action Decade 2021-2030 is organized into 7 sections and has 3 annexes.
ARDB Director General Inspects Cashew Harvesting and Warehouses in Kampong Thom and Preah Vihear Provinces
(Preah Vihear): On the afternoon of April 7, 2023, Dr. Kao Thach, Royal Government Delegate in charge of the Director General of the Rural Development Bank (ARDB) and his colleagues inspected the cashew harvest and inspected the warehouse. Cashew stock at 2 locations:
* First: Cashew cultivation farm, located in Ta Minh village, Kraya commune, Santuk district, Kampong Thom province. The farm is harvesting 580 hectares of cultivated land. For 2023, the farm has harvested 130 tons.
* Second: Santana Agro Pradak Ek Co., Ltd. is located in Chi Ork Village, Romney Commune, Rovieng District, Preah Vihear Province. Currently, the company is cultivating and harvesting cashew nuts on 1,000 hectares, and the company has processed cashews to supply the domestic market and export to China, Europe and so on. In addition, the company has a warehouse that can hold up to 5,000 tons for processing and processing.
Currently, according to the cashew association report, the total area under cashew cultivation in Preah Vihear province is 84,391 hectares and there are 43 cashew farming communities.
In the future, Dr. Kao Thach will visit the cashew community and cashew collection companies in some provinces, including Kampong Thom, Preah Vihear, Kratie and Stung Treng.
