Owners of 9 Restaurants in Pursat City Decide Not to Sell Wild Meat to Customers
(Pursat): By promoting awareness of the value of wildlife and the legal challenges of taking wildlife meat for sale to customers, nine restaurant owners in Pursat have committed Absolutely do not sell food made from wild meat to customers, even if customers order and give expensive prices.
With the launch of the Zero Trap Campaign in Pursat, in addition to the owners of the above nine restaurants, students and residents have promised to bring their awareness of the benefits of natural resources and wildlife to their families, relatives and friends. Also.
To date, there are more than 50 restaurants in seven provinces: Kratie, Stung Treng, Preah Vihear, Ratanakkiri, Mondulkiri and Pursat. Wildlife meat in protected areas and wildlife conservation.
On the morning of April 7, 2023, on the occasion of the opening of the second phase of the Zero Trap Campaign in Pursat Province, Mr. Net Pheaktra, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Environment and Chairman of the Zero Trap Campaign, presented a certificate of appreciation to Restaurant owners also put up stickers advertising the importance of wildlife in restaurants.
He said that Pursat has a lot of potential and the protection of forests and forests will make people in areas where wildlife is present will have economic growth.
The nine restaurants include: Happy Nay Restaurant, Mohaleap Restaurant, Chan Mony Restaurant, Mony Chan Sok San Restaurant, Seven Luck Restaurant, Zara Cafe Restaurant, Stung Meas Restaurant, Slamas Entertainment Center Restaurant, Mlup Svay Restaurant and Lagosi Coffee Restaurant.
