Leaders of Reachsey Association Visit and Distribute to 30 Families in 2 Communes in Prey Nob District, Preah Sihanouk Province
(Preah Sihanouk): Mr. Sum Saroeun, President of the Reach Sey Association and leaders of the Reach Sey Association presided over a meeting to visit the elderly people in O'Chrov commune, Prey Nob district, Preah Sihanouk province. This program took place in the morning and afternoon of April 6, 2023, located in O'Chrov commune and Boeung Ta Prohm commune, Prey Nob district, Sihanoukville province.
On that occasion, Mr. Sum Saroeun reminded all people to support Samdech Techo Hun Sen as the Prime Ministerial candidate for the 7th legislature of the National Assembly and to fully support Dr. Hun Manet as the Prime Ministerial candidate for the future. He added that Buddhism is the state religion, but the Royal Government of Cambodia and leaders at all levels do not discriminate on the basis of race or color.
It should be noted that during this meeting, Mr. Sum Saroeun brought some donations from the Reachsey Association of Sihanoukville Branch to the Preah Vihear Management Committee in 2 communes, O'Chrov and Boeung Ta Prohm communes in Prey Nob district. Sihanoukville Province for repair, construction, expansion of old temples that are dilapidated to be beautiful and strong again.
(Phnom Penh): The Cambodian Organization of the Elderly, in collaboration with the Cambodian Network of the Elderly, on April 7, 2023, celebrated the World Health Day under the theme "Good Health for All Ages" to contribute to raising awareness. Especially the elderly to move towards universal health coverage.
Please be informed that World Health Day is an important event organized in order to contribute to raise awareness and collect input from senior representatives of the 14 capitals and provinces of the Kingdom of Cambodia related to their priority needs. In terms of health, it aims to promote access to a good care system and health services that are suitable for people of all ages, especially the elderly, towards global health coverage.
On the occasion of this day, there will be the participation of representatives of the elderly and sharing from representatives of relevant ministries, specialized departments and the World Health Organization around the strategy to reduce diseases and deaths caused by non-communicable diseases and other public health problems and Progress of Health Insurance Towards Global Health Coverage in Cambodia's Social Protection System.
The JICA Cambodia Office would like to thank all the stakeholders for their support and cooperation in assisting Haruko in fulfilling her mission, and requested that she continue to support and cooperate with all JICA activities. Ministry of Environment launches campaign to reduce the use of plastic bags and promote environmentally friendly baskets
(Kratie): Mr. Ken Serey Ratha, Director General of the General Department of Environmental Knowledge and Information of the Ministry of Environment, on April 7, 2023, organized a campaign to reduce the use of plastic bags and promote environmental baskets in Kratie province.
The event was attended by Mr. Hang Chandy, Deputy Governor of Kratie Province and about 300 relevant departments, youths and students in front of Samaki Market, Kratie City.
Mr. Hang Chandy said that at present, countries all over the world are experiencing serious environmental problems, especially plastic waste, which has caused serious harm to the world, society, family and future generations.
In fact, in Kratie province, the consumption of food materials and other products has left a lot of waste from day to day and has increased significantly due to the growing rate of population demand and the storage and packaging of waste. Garbage in plastic bags is not good, more than 3 tons / day.
He also handed over the book Cambodia, My Motherland, Environmental Water Bottles and Environmental Baskets to the provincial leaders, relevant departments, commune chiefs and participants in the ceremony, as well as distributed to the people and traders in Samaki Market to contribute to reducing plastic bags in daily life. Their day, too.
